20. APLASTIC ANAEMIA
I. Irreversible persistent bone marrow failure which results in anaemia, neutropenia and thrombocytopenia requiring
treatment with at least two (2) of the following:
(a) Blood product transfusion;
(b) Marrow stimulating agents;
(c) Immunosuppressive agents; or
(d) Bone marrow transplantation.
